{"agent":"impl-descriptor-v2","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_validate_surfaces` decides whether a section “has values” by truthiness (`any(v for k, v in vars(sec).items() if k != \"none\")`), so legitimate TOML values that are falsy are treated as absence. For example, a descriptor containing `[caps] mcp_tool_cap = 0` (a zero MCP-tool cap is a documented cap, not absence) is built into a `Caps` section with `mcp_tool_cap == 0`, then `_validate_surfaces` computes `has_values == False`, sees `none == False`, and raises `[caps] is empty: omit it or say none = true`. The same truthiness test also lets contradictory descriptors pass: `[caps] none = true` plus `mcp_tool_cap = 0` is accepted because the zero value is ignored, even though `none = true` and a supplied cap contradict the three-valued “absent / none=true / value” loading rule.","digest":"5ab8a53de323ed10","location":"ddflow/services/harnessreg.py:_validate_surfaces","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/harnessreg.py:_validate_surfaces"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The test claims to verify that “all v2 sections parse,” but it includes `[meters]` and `[telemetry]` in the TOML and then never asserts anything about `h.meters` or `h.telemetry` (and it only samples a few keys from the other sections). If the loader silently ignores `[meters]` and `[telemetry]`, returning `None` for them, this test still passes, so it does not actually enforce that the v2 sections are parsed and exposed as intended.","digest":"323a7c8ee066b082","location":"tests/test_harness_descriptor_v2.py:test_all_v2_sections_parse","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_harness_descriptor_v2.py:test_all_v2_sections_parse"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":16082,"diff_sha":"1e50074f69b6e364f88ef6b34829546955ad343f53d045766c5190c6175cb238","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":966.2,"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"7f583d4f02ca9890","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/P-agent-parity.descriptor-v2.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261029T214140Z-2d6c52e2.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"0b3edf7bfc234760c07b58dd21a8bbec0122596c","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/harnessreg.py":"100644 71d7d012e32dfdfcb8481408d5fa76fffaea8ad4","ddflow/services/harnessv2.py":"100644 0bb36e99effb1e0b33c15ecc4c5c94b078c272db","docs/ddflow/adding-a-harness.md":"100644 3799c658b8ec5a7115ea923d4ca74dc3ee22db29","tests/test_harness_descriptor_v2.py":"100644 aba23736538969503d813ba2f4d054372bf843c9"},"reviewer":"qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/harnessreg.py:_validate_surfaces","tests/test_harness_descriptor_v2.py:test_all_v2_sections_parse"],"tree_sha":"0b3edf7bfc23+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e566e292ebee21273526295af","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":113129,"schema":1,"subject":"P-agent-parity.descriptor-v2","ts":"2026-10-29T22:02:46.488845Z"}
